IMPORT prelude

-- Defamation Act 1957 (Singapore) -- when slander and malicious falsehood are actionable without proof of special damage
-- (ss 3-6), unintentional defamation and the offer of amends (s 7), the partial-truth rules for justification and fair comment
-- (ss 8, 9), apology in mitigation (s 10(1)), reports of court proceedings (s 11), the newspaper Schedule privilege and what a
-- "newspaper" is (ss 2, 12, 13 and the Schedule), election statements (s 14) and indemnity agreements (s 15).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DA1957.txt. The deposit's cover says it
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; its page header reads "Informal Consolidation - version in
-- force from 1/4/2022". The latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 25 of 2021 (wef 01/04/2022), which appears on ss 5, 6,
-- 7, 8, 10, 12, 16-19. Section numbers follow the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone in Singapore who posts, forwards, speaks or prints something
-- unflattering about another person, or is on the receiving end of it, is inside this Act. An automated count found none of the
-- 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by its slug title; that count undercounts Acts cited by short or older titles and is
-- not a measure of importance. SCOPED to the rules an individual meets in a dispute. Not encoded: the definitions of
-- "telecommunication" and "words" beyond their use here, s 7(4) (the High Court's power over the steps and costs of an accepted
-- offer) beyond a comment, s 10(2) (newspaper payment into court), s 12(4), the procedural ss 16-20 (other damages recovered,
-- consolidation, separate assessment, severance), and s 21 (criminal law untouched) beyond a comment.
--
-- The Act modifies the common law of libel and slander; it does not restate it. Where a rule below needs a common-law premise
-- (for example that libel is actionable without special damage), the comment says it is an INFERENCE, not text of this Act.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Defamation Act 1957 -- defamation`

§§ `3, 4, 5 -- slander actionable without special damage`

-- s 3: "the broadcasting of words by means of telecommunication shall be treated as publication in a permanent form."
-- s 2: "broadcasting by means of telecommunication" means "publication for general reception by means of telecommunication";
-- "words" includes "pictures, visual images, gestures and other methods of signifying meaning".
-- s 4: "Words spoken and published which impute unchastity or adultery to any woman or girl shall not require special damage to
-- render them actionable."
-- s 5: words "calculated to disparage the claimant in any office, profession, calling, trade or business held or carried on by
-- him at the time of the publication" -- no need to allege or prove special damage "whether or not the words are spoken of the
-- claimant in the way of his office".
-- INFERENCE (common law, not this Act): a statement in permanent form is libel and is actionable without special damage; a
-- transient one is slander and needs special damage unless an exception applies.
DECLARE Form IS ONE OF
    `spoken words`
    `a gesture`
    `writing`
    `a broadcast for general reception`

GIVEN `the form` IS A Form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the form is permanent` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `writing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a broadcast for general reception` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Statement HAS
    `form of publication` IS A Form
    `imputes unchastity or adultery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant is a woman or girl` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disparages the claimant in an office or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant held that office or business at publication` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the statement` IS A Statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `actionable without proof of special damage` IF
        `the form is permanent` (`the statement`'s `form of publication`)
    OR  (`the statement`'s `imputes unchastity or adultery` AND `the statement`'s `the claimant is a woman or girl`)
    OR  (`the statement`'s `disparages the claimant in an office or business`
         AND `the statement`'s `the claimant held that office or business at publication`)

§§ `6 -- slander of title, slander of goods and other malicious falsehood`

-- s 6(1): no need "to allege or prove special damage" (a) "if the words ... are calculated to cause pecuniary damage to the
-- claimant and are published in writing or other permanent form"; or (b) if they are "calculated to cause pecuniary damage to
-- the claimant in respect of any office, profession, calling, trade or business held or carried on by him at the time of the
-- publication". (2): s 3 applies, so a broadcast is a permanent form.
DECLARE Falsehood HAS
    `form of the falsehood` IS A Form
    `calculated to cause pecuniary damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of a business held at publication` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the falsehood` IS A Falsehood
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the falsehood needs no proof of special damage` IF
        `the falsehood`'s `calculated to cause pecuniary damage`
    AND (    `the form is permanent` (`the falsehood`'s `form of the falsehood`)
         OR  `the falsehood`'s `in respect of a business held at publication`)

§§ `7 -- unintentional defamation and the offer of amends`

-- s 7(5): words are published "innocently" "if and only if" (a) the publisher "did not intend to publish them of and concerning
-- that other person, and did not know of circumstances by virtue of which they might be understood to refer to him"; or (b)
-- "the words were not defamatory on the face of them, and the publisher did not know of circumstances by virtue of which they
-- might be understood to be defamatory of that other person", "and in either case that the publisher exercised all reasonable
-- care in relation to the publication".
DECLARE Publisher HAS
    `intended to refer to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew circumstances making the words refer to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the words were defamatory on their face` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew circumstances making the words defamatory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exercised all reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the publisher` IS A Publisher
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the words were published innocently` IF
        (    ((NOT `the publisher`'s `intended to refer to the claimant`)
              AND (NOT `the publisher`'s `knew circumstances making the words refer to the claimant`))
         OR  ((NOT `the publisher`'s `the words were defamatory on their face`)
              AND (NOT `the publisher`'s `knew circumstances making the words defamatory`)))
    AND `the publisher`'s `exercised all reasonable care`

-- s 7(2): the offer "must be expressed to be made for the purposes of this section, and must be accompanied by an affidavit
-- specifying the facts relied upon"; and for the s 7(1)(b) defence "no evidence, other than evidence of facts specified in the
-- affidavit, shall be admissible". (3): the offer is to publish "a suitable correction" and "a sufficient apology" and to notify
-- those to whom copies were distributed.
-- s 7(1)(a): if the offer "is accepted by the party aggrieved and is duly performed, no proceedings for libel or slander shall be
-- taken or continued" against the offeror (but not against others jointly responsible).
-- s 7(1)(b): if NOT accepted, it is a defence to prove that the words "were published by the defendant or were published by the
-- defendant innocently in relation to the claimant and that the offer was made as soon as practicable after the defendant
-- received notice ... and has not been withdrawn". Read literally, the first limb ("were published by the defendant") is met by
-- every defendant; this encoding takes the evident sense, innocent publication. That is a reading, not the text.
-- s 7(6): (1)(b) does not apply to words "of which he is not the author unless he proves that the words were written by the
-- author without malice".
-- s 7(4) (not encoded): on acceptance, disputes about the steps go to the General Division of the High Court, "whose decision
-- shall be final", and costs may be ordered "on an indemnity basis".
DECLARE Offer HAS
    `expressed to be made under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by an affidavit of the facts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made as soon as practicable after notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `duly performed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer is a valid offer of amends` IF
    `the offer`'s `expressed to be made under section 7` AND `the offer`'s `accompanied by an affidavit of the facts`

GIVEN `the offer` IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings against the offeror are barred` IF
        `the offer is a valid offer of amends` `the offer`
    AND `the offer`'s `accepted`
    AND `the offer`'s `duly performed`

GIVEN `the publisher` IS A Publisher, `the offer` IS AN Offer, `the defendant is the author` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the author wrote without malice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer of amends defence is available` IF
        `the words were published innocently` `the publisher`
    AND `the offer is a valid offer of amends` `the offer`
    AND (NOT `the offer`'s `accepted`)
    AND `the offer`'s `made as soon as practicable after notice`
    AND (NOT `the offer`'s `withdrawn`)
    AND (`the defendant is the author` OR `proved the author wrote without malice`)

§§ `8, 9 -- partial truth: justification and fair comment`

-- s 8: where the words contain "2 or more distinct charges", justification "shall not fail by reason only that the truth of
-- every charge is not proved if the words not proved to be true do not materially injure the claimant's reputation having
-- regard to the truth of the remaining charges".
-- INFERENCE: "having regard to the truth of the remaining charges" presupposes at least one charge proved. With a single
-- charge, s 8 does not help; the charge must be proved.
GIVEN `distinct charges` IS A NUMBER, `charges proved true` IS A NUMBER, `the unproved charges materially injure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `justification does not fail` IF
        `charges proved true` AT LEAST `distinct charges`
    OR  (    `distinct charges` AT LEAST 2
         AND `charges proved true` AT LEAST 1
         AND (NOT `the unproved charges materially injure`))

-- s 9: where words are "partly of allegations of fact and partly of expression of opinion, a defence of fair comment shall not
-- fail by reason only that the truth of every allegation of fact is not proved if the expression of opinion is fair comment
-- having regard to such of the facts ... as are proved". The other elements of fair comment are common law and not encoded.
GIVEN `every fact proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the opinion is fair on the facts proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fair comment is not defeated by unproved facts` IF
    `every fact proved` OR `the opinion is fair on the facts proved`

§§ `10(1) -- apology in mitigation of damages`

-- s 10(1): the defendant may, "after notice in writing of his intention to do so duly given to the claimant at the time of
-- filing his written statement of his case", give in evidence in mitigation "that he made or offered an apology ... before the
-- commencement of the action or, where the action was commenced before there was an opportunity of making or offering such
-- apology, as soon afterwards as he had an opportunity of doing so".
GIVEN `gave written notice when filing the statement of case` IS A BOOLEAN, `apologised before the action began` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the action began before any opportunity to apologise` IS A BOOLEAN, `apologised at the first opportunity after` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the apology may be given in mitigation` IF
        `gave written notice when filing the statement of case`
    AND (    `apologised before the action began`
         OR  (`the action began before any opportunity to apologise` AND `apologised at the first opportunity after`))

§§ `11 -- reports of judicial proceedings`

-- s 11(1): "A fair and accurate and contemporaneous report of proceedings publicly heard before any court lawfully exercising
-- judicial authority within Singapore and of the judgment, sentence or finding of any such court shall be absolutely
-- privileged ... although such judgment, sentence or finding is subsequently reversed, quashed or varied, unless at the time
-- of the publication ... the defendant ... knew or ought to have known of such reversal, quashing or variation."
-- (2): nothing authorises "any blasphemous, seditious or indecent matter or ... any matter the publication of which is
-- prohibited by law".
DECLARE CourtReport HAS
    `fair and accurate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contemporaneous` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of proceedings publicly heard` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of a court within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the publisher knew or ought to have known of a reversal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains blasphemous, seditious, indecent or prohibited matter` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the report` IS A CourtReport
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court report is absolutely privileged` IF
        `the report`'s `fair and accurate`
    AND `the report`'s `contemporaneous`
    AND `the report`'s `of proceedings publicly heard`
    AND `the report`'s `of a court within Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the report`'s `the publisher knew or ought to have known of a reversal`)
    AND (NOT `the report`'s `contains blasphemous, seditious, indecent or prohibited matter`)

§§ `2, 12, 13 and the Schedule -- qualified privilege of newspapers`

-- s 2: "newspaper" means "any paper containing public news or observations thereon or consisting wholly or mainly of
-- advertisements which is printed for sale and is published in Singapore either periodically or in parts or numbers at
-- intervals not exceeding 36 days".
GIVEN `contains public news or advertisements` IS A BOOLEAN, `printed for sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `published in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days between issues` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a newspaper` IF
        `contains public news or advertisements`
    AND `printed for sale`
    AND `published in Singapore`
    AND `days between issues` AT MOST 36

-- Schedule Part 1 ("privileged without explanation or contradiction"): fair and accurate reports of Commonwealth legislatures
-- outside Singapore, international organisations and conferences, Commonwealth courts outside Singapore, public inquiries; copies
-- of public registers; notices by courts and public officers. Part 2 ("subject to explanation or contradiction"): findings of
-- arts, science, religion, learning, trade, professional and sporting associations about their members; public meetings in
-- Singapore; statutory inquiries and bodies; general meetings of companies (not private companies); notices for the
-- information of the public by the Government or a public officer or authority.
DECLARE ScheduleMatter IS ONE OF
    `a report of a foreign Commonwealth parliament`
    `a copy of a public register entry`
    `a court notice`
    `a report of a professional body's disciplinary finding`
    `a report of a public meeting`
    `a report of a public company's general meeting`
    `a Government notice to the public`
    `a report of a private company's general meeting`
    `a rumour from a private conversation`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A ScheduleMatter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in Part 1 of the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `a report of a foreign Commonwealth parliament` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a copy of a public register entry` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court notice` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the matter` IS A ScheduleMatter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in Part 2 of the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `a report of a professional body's disciplinary finding` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a report of a public meeting` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a report of a public company's general meeting` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Government notice to the public` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 12(1): publication "in a newspaper" of Schedule matter "shall be privileged unless the publication is proved to be made with
-- malice". (2): for Part 2 matter, no defence if the claimant asked the defendant to publish "a reasonable letter or statement by
-- way of explanation or contradiction" and the defendant "has refused or neglected to do so, or has done so in a manner not
-- adequate or not reasonable". (3): no protection for blasphemous, seditious, indecent or prohibited matter, "or of any matter
-- which is not of public concern and the publication of which is not for the public benefit".
-- s 13(1): the Act applies to matter broadcast "by means of a broadcasting station within Singapore" as to a newspaper; (3) a
-- broadcasting station is one authorised or licensed by law.
-- Read literally, s 12(3) removes protection only where the matter is BOTH not of public concern AND not for the public benefit.
-- This encoding follows the literal words; whether a court reads it that way was not checked.
DECLARE NewsItem HAS
    `in a newspaper or on a licensed Singapore broadcasting station` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved to be made with malice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant asked for an explanation to be published` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the publisher refused or did it inadequately` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of public concern` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for the public benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains forbidden matter` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the matter` IS A ScheduleMatter, `the item` IS A NewsItem
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the newspaper privilege applies` IF
        `the item`'s `in a newspaper or on a licensed Singapore broadcasting station`
    AND (`is in Part 1 of the Schedule` `the matter` OR `is in Part 2 of the Schedule` `the matter`)
    AND (NOT `the item`'s `proved to be made with malice`)
    AND (NOT (    `is in Part 2 of the Schedule` `the matter`
              AND `the item`'s `the claimant asked for an explanation to be published`
              AND `the item`'s `the publisher refused or did it inadequately`))
    AND (NOT ((NOT `the item`'s `of public concern`) AND (NOT `the item`'s `for the public benefit`)))
    AND (NOT `the item`'s `contains forbidden matter`)

§§ `14, 15 -- elections and indemnities`

-- s 14: a defamatory statement "published by or on behalf of a candidate in any election to the office of President or to
-- Parliament or other elected or partially elected body shall not be deemed to be published on a privileged occasion on the
-- ground that it is material to a question in issue in the election, whether or not the person by whom it is published is
-- qualified to vote".
GIVEN `published by or for a candidate in an election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `election materiality can found privilege` IF
    NOT `published by or for a candidate in an election`

-- s 15: an agreement to indemnify against civil liability for libel "shall not be unlawful unless at the time of the
-- publication that person knows that the matter is defamatory and does not reasonably believe there is a good defence".
GIVEN `knew the matter was defamatory` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably believed there was a good defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the indemnity agreement is lawful` IF
    NOT (`knew the matter was defamatory` AND (NOT `reasonably believed there was a good defence`))

-- s 21: nothing in this Act "affects the provisions of the Penal Code 1871 or any other written law relating to criminal
-- offences or applies to any prosecution for a criminal offence". Not encoded.
